id: pm-brief-nkfr
title: Gate durable PM project health in CI on pm CLI 2026.8.6
description: "Resolve the current pm CLI and pm-changelog toolchain in the lockfile and run pm health --strict-exit immediately after dependency installation. The gate catches durable checkout-visible tracker corruption, stale in-progress work, tracked runtime state, and merge evidence present in the clone. It is explicitly not lossless merge attestation because receipts are clone-local and repair can erase drift; upstream pm-cli issues 921 and 922 track those limitations."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-06T23:01:17.085Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-06T23:31:16.024Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-06T23:01:48.302Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-06T23:01:48.302Z"
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: "package-lock resolves pm CLI and pm-changelog 2026.8.6; the workflow runs the local pm binary with --strict-exit before package checks; comments state exact detected and undetected scope and link upstream 921 and 922; pm health, release:check, and changelog:check pass; changed paths and verification are linked"
severity: high
environment: GitHub Actions CI and local release gate on pm CLI 2026.8.6
resolution: "Locked the current toolchain, refreshed the tracked merge fence where pm CLI 2026.8.6 required it, and added the accurately scoped strict health step before package validation."
expected_result: A checkout-visible PM health failure stops CI with a non-zero exit without claiming to detect every silently discarded peer edit.
actual_result: "The lock resolves pm CLI and pm-changelog 2026.8.6, the workflow runs the installed binary with strict exit and accurate limitation comments, local strict health exits 0, and the package release gate passed at the updated dependency resolution."
